# J10 — Autonomy dial
# Ctrl+↑ / Ctrl+↓ and the autonomy/posture verb across recon/hunt/confirm/fix.
# The ⛭ chip must show ⚠ only when it actually throttles the walker; raising
# the dial must never forge phase progress.
name: Autonomy dial
env: KUZUSHI_REDUCED_MOTION=1 KUZUSHI_SKIP_ONBOARDING=1
launch: --target @TMP_TARGET
wait-for: 30 kuzushi>
snap: dial-default
expect: ⛭
ask: Default posture — does the ⛭ chip show the default rung (fix/unconstrained) with no ⚠ when nothing is throttled?
submit: autonomy recon
wait: 2
snap: dial-recon
expect: recon
ask: Lowered to recon — does the chip update immediately, and does a ⚠ appear ONLY if the current phase walker is actually throttled by the new ceiling?
keys: C-Up
wait: 2
snap: dial-ctrl-up
ask: Ctrl+↑ chord — did the rung raise by exactly one step, and is the change announced (chip + event line), not silent?
keys: C-Down C-Down
wait: 2
snap: dial-ctrl-down
ask: Ctrl+↓ twice — same honesty check downward; did the phase chip (組 …) stay UNCHANGED (raising/lowering the dial must not forge phase progress)?
submit: posture fix
wait: 2
snap: dial-back-to-fix
expect: fix
